->manam k8s lo oka pod lo cont create chestamu, a cont ki port istunnam kani, host port ekkada ivvadam ledu- so app ni access cheyyalemu
->in order to access app frm cont we need to expose it(using services we can expose it)
->k8s svc is used to expose our containers
->there are 3 types of svc's
    i)ClusterIP
    ii)NodePort
    iii)LoadBalancer
->ClusterIP = to access cont within the same server
    for db's,logs,scripts....
    we get static-ip
    using curl cmd we can chk(curl static-ip=ey server lo create chesthey danloney access chesukovali)
->NodePort = to access cont within the same server n host/node/instance/server
    nodeport range - 30,000 to 32,767
    we get static-ip,nodeport
    to access app server_ip:range
    we can access app internally n externally(server_ip:port)
IQ - why shd be that particular range for a nodeport service?
scenario - suppose mana app 2 nodes lo run avutundi, a cont ki nodeport thoney create chesamu. users ki 2 server ip's ichamu but ey server aina vadachu.Lst's assume oka server ey use chestunaru anukundam, appudu req's anni a server ki ey veltai so app down ayye chance undi.
so loadbalancer use chesthey traffic equal ga veltadi
->LoadBalancer = to expose our app's we use loadbalancer
    using loadbalancer we'n access app internally n externally
    we get static-ip,nodeport n dns
IQ - what is dif b/w nodeport n loadbalancer?
nodeport req's anni oka server ki ey veltai, ade loadbalancer lo aithey req's distribute avutai
PRACTICAL IMPLEMENTATION OF SERVCIES
1. clusterIP
->Create a server vth t3micro, 25gb n attach iam role also(which created previously)
->install kops,attach s3 bucket also n install kubectl 
->create a pod
vim pod.yml
    apiVersion : v1
    kind: Pod
    metadata: 
      name: pod1
      labels:
        app:swiggy
    spec:
      containers:
        - name: cont1
          image: shaikmustafa/dm
          ports:
            - containerPort: 80
NOTE - It's mandatory to give label to every pod
->create a service(service name can be anything)
vim myservice.yml
apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  -name: myservice
spec:
  type: ClusterIP
  selector:
    app: swiggy
  ports:
    - port: 1111
      targetPort: 80
NOTE - 1 to access app curl ip:1111
       2 port= svc port, targetport = app port
       3 targetport lo p capital
explanation - oka pod lo chala conts unnai, oka cont ni ip:1111 tho access chesamu- appudu a cont ki req ela veltadi antey, 1st mana browser nunchi req svc ki veltadi, a svc nunchi particular target cont ki veltadi
